 "notes": [
  "The byline 'Darth Vader \"The Dark\" Lord of The Sith' is a prank name; the deck is credited to the DeckTech handle The Dark as plain text (no player page), as with his other DeckTech decks (e.g. 18120, 18156, 18194, 18394).",
  "Starting cards as posted under 'Starting (5)': Hidden Base / Systems Will Slip Through Your Fingers, Rendezvous Point, Heading For The Medical Frigate, Staging Areas and Squadron Assignments; these count toward the 60. The sixth starting line, 'HB Indicator (usually Kessel or Hoth)', is the Hidden Base system; the Locations header says it is counted there, so it is not a separate card.",
  "Posted 4 August 2001 with no Coruscant-set cards, so the format is Premiere - Tatooine.",
  "The deck totals 61 as published. The Locations header says 15, but 16 locations are listed.",
  "Generic systems dested to the Light printings: Tatooine (Light) (Premiere), Hoth (Light), Endor (Light), Dagobah (Light).",
  "Posted 'Hidden Base / Systems Will Slip Trough Your Fingers', 'General Calrissan', 'Lengendary Starfighter', 'Dantooin' and 'Nebulon B-Frigate' are spelling slips (Nebulon-B Frigate).",
  "Posted 'Collision' dested Collision!; 'Hoth Echo Docking Bay' Hoth: Echo Docking Bay; 'Yavin 4 Docking Bay' Yavin 4: Docking Bay.",
  "This is an earlier version of the same player's Hidden Base deck 18194 (Hidden Base v 2)."
 ],
